{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"recursion","title":"Recursion","group":"","order":4,"html":"<p>A Function calls itself directly or indirectly</p>\n<p>Direct Method:</p>\n<p>def func();</p>\n<ul>\n<li>func()</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Indirect Method</p>\n<p>def fun1():</p>\n<ul>\n<li>fun2()</li>\n</ul>\n<p>def fun2();</p>\n<ul>\n<li>fun1()</li>\n</ul>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def fun():\n  for i in range(1):\n    print(\"GFG\")\n    break\n\nfun()</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Recursion Background</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def fun1():\n  print(\"Function 1 is called\")\n\nfun1()</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def fun2():\n  print(\"Before Function 1\")\n  fun1()\n  print(\"After Function 1\")\n\nprint(\"Before Function 2\")\nfun2()\nprint(\"After Function 2\")</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Typical structure of Reecursive Functions</h3>\n<p>def fun(...):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>base cases</li>\n<li>Recursive cal : with atleast one change to parameter so that call approches towards base case</li>\n</ul>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Applications of Recursion</h3>\n<p>1. Many algorithm techniques are based on recursive</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dynamic Programming</li>\n<li>Backtracking</li>\n<li>Divide and Conquer (Binary Search, Merge Sort, Quick Sort)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>2. Many Problems inherently recursive</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tower of Hanoi</li>\n<li>DFS based traversals (DFS of graph and Inorder, Post Order, Pre Order traverse)</li>\n</ul>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Factorial\n\ndef fact(n):\n  if n == 0:    # base case\n    return 1\n  return n * fact(n-1) # recursive case\n\nfact(5)\n\n# Note : Don't use n == 1 because it goes to -ve infinity</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Fibbonacci : nth value of series\n\n# 0 1 1 2 3 5 8 12 20\n\ndef fib(n):\n  if n == 0 or n == 1:\n    return n\n  return fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)\n\nfib(10)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Tail Recursion</h3>\n<p>A recursive function is called tail recursive if the function does not do anything after the last recursive call.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def fun(n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return\n  print(n)\n  fun(n-1)   # Tail Recursive function\n\nfun(5)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Not Tail Recursion\n\ndef fun(n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return\n  fun(n-1)\n  print(n)   # Not Tail Recursive function\n\nfun(5)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Removing Recursion</h3>\n<p>1. Replace if with while</p>\n<p>2. Change value of parameters at the end of loop</p>\n<p>Examples of Tail Recursive Functions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Quick Sort</li>\n<li>Post Order Tree Traversal</li>\n</ul>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def fun(n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return\n  print(n, end = ' ')\n  fun(n-1)\n  print(n, end = ' ')\n\nfun(4)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def fun(n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return\n  fun(n-1)\n  print(n, end = ' ')\n  fun(n-1)\n\nfun(4)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Calculates the number of times you can divide n by 2\n\ndef fun(n):\n  if n &lt;= 1:\n    return 0\n  else:\n    return 1 + fun(n//2)\n\nfun(16)\n\n# What does this funtion do in general for n &gt;= 1 ?\n\n# log_2(n)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Shows the Binary Representaion of a number\n\ndef fun(n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return\n  fun(n//2)\n  print(n%2, end = '')\n\nfun(13)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Print 1 to N &amp; N to 1</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> n = 4<br><strong>Output:</strong> 1 2 3 4</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># 1 to N\n\ndef print1toN(n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return\n  print1toN(n-1)\n  print(n, end = ' ')\n\nprint1toN(4)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># N to 1\n\ndef printNto1(n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return\n  print(n, end = ' ')\n  printNto1(n-1)\n\nprintNto1(4)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Sum of Digits</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> n = 253<br><strong>Output:</strong> 10</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def fun(n):\n  if n &lt; 10:\n    return n\n  return fun(n//10) + n % 10\n\nfun(253)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Palindrome Check</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> 'aabbaa'</p>\n</div>\n<p>O/p : False</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def palin(str, start, end):\n  if start &gt;= end:\n    return True\n  return str[start] == str[end] and palin(str, start+1, end-1)\n\npalin('aabbaa', 0, 5)</code></pre></figure></section>"}